# Accepted divergences from the canonical .ci/breakpoint/ in rediacc/console.
#
# EMPTY IS THE CORRECT STATE FOR THE CANONICAL REPO. This file exists for
# repositories that VENDORED breakpoint and have a genuine, repo-specific reason
# to carry a modified copy of one of the frozen files.
#
# Before adding an entry, try the other three options first. In order of
# preference:
#   1. Revert your local edit.
#   2. Land the change in rediacc/console, run check-breakpoint-drift.sh --write
#      there, and re-vendor here with sync-breakpoint.sh. This is nearly always
#      the right answer: breakpoint is meant to be one implementation.
#   3. Move the varying value into breakpoint.conf, which is not frozen and is
#      the sanctioned per-repo edit point.
#   4. Only then, accept the divergence here.
#
# FORMAT -- a BLOCKER comment immediately above each accepted path:
#
#   # BLOCKER: <>=30 chars naming what is different about THIS repo AND why the
#   #          canonical copy cannot carry the change>
#   scripts/install-vnc-desktop.sh
#
# Validated by lib/breakpoint-blocker.sh: a reason shorter than 30 characters,
# or one matching the banned-phrase list ("tbd", "wip", "ok", "later", ...), is
# rejected. So is an entry naming a path that is not in MANIFEST.sha256 -- a
# stale accept is reported as a hard failure rather than lingering forever,
# which is the lesson from the 101 dead entries documented in
# docs/agent-reference/suppressions.md.
